    "Dry run" : {

    },
    "Duplicates are detected by exact file content — identical bytes are collapsed to one. Conversations are grouped by subject with reply/forward prefixes stripped, then ordered by date. This is subject-based threading: the archive doesn't store the email Message-ID / In-Reply-To headers that would let two unrelated \"Re: update\" chains be told apart, so treat a thread as a strong grouping, not a guarantee." : {

